  "description": "LUYFAN crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H111 N2 O15 S8 Yb3,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),3.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.428-3.447 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.59-99.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H111N2O15S8Yb3·4(dmf)·3.5(H2O) (crystal C99H147N6O22.5S8Yb3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
